/* chunk_stress.plsw -- AST-pool stress fixture for reg-rs.
 *
 * Purpose: drive the compiler's AST node pool past the
 * pre-fix CHUNK_MAX=16 (2,176-node) ceiling so the
 * capacity-and-test saga's bump to CHUNK_MAX=128 is
 * exercised by `just test`. Without this fixture, the
 * 2026-05-12 capacity regression that broke shipped main
 * (sno_lex.plsw / sno_exec.plsw failing with "AST pool
 * exhausted") would not have been caught by reg-rs.
 *
 * See:
 *   - tools/briefs/dcpls-ast-chunk-capacity-and-test.md
 *     (mike, 2026-05-12)
 *   - docs/memory-audit-2026-05-12.md (per-input peaks)
 *
 * Expected peak: ~7,500-8,000 AST nodes during compile
 * (80 DCLs + 60 PROCs * 30 stmts/PROC + MAIN). The
 * helper procs are never called; MAIN prints "ok" and exits.
 *
 * Generated by /tmp/gen-chunk-stress.py (commit message
 * has the parameters). Regenerate with the same script if
 * the fixture needs resizing, then re-bootstrap goldens
 * via `just test-bootstrap-goldens`.
 */

/* --- Globals --- */
